# Trivy filesystem-scan exceptions. Each entry needs a reason and the date it
# was added — see docs/DEPLOY.md / scripts/audit-gate.mjs for the equivalent
# npm-side allowlist and its house rules (this file has no automated
# staleness check, so review these by hand alongside that one).

# CVE-2026-59873 — node-tar: Denial of Service via crafted gzip bomb (tar@6.2.1).
# Same root cause and same "not affected" evidence as the tar entries in
# scripts/audit-gate.mjs (added 2026-08-28): every copy of tar@6.2.1 traces to
# @taskboard/desktop's native-module build tooling (get-windows's
# @mapbox/node-pre-gyp / node-gyp chain), which only ever extracts prebuilt
# binaries get-windows fetches from its own GitHub releases — never an
# attacker-supplied archive — and never ships in the packaged app or runs in
# any deployed service. Review alongside the audit-gate.mjs entries.
CVE-2026-59873
